('area:les-3-vallees','routes','note',4,'The two ends of the area, each reached by gondola with no piste home.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','routes.rows.4.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','routes','note',5,'Even by this measure the corners of the area are a long way apart: from Moriond, Orelle takes {{m:all.moriond.orelle|w}} lift rides going south and {{m:all.orelle.moriond|w}} coming back.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','routes.after'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','heading',0,'The eight resorts compared','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.h2'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',0,'The pass covers places as different as Brides-les-Bains, a spa town with no pistes of its own, and Val Thorens, where every lift starts above 2,000 m. Their place on the ridge decides how quickly the rest of the area can be reached.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.intro'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','caption',0,'Resorts on the Les 3 Vallées pass','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.caption'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',1,'Linked; four villages from Le Praz to 1850','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.0.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',0,'Holds the most drag lifts in the area; the Saulire cable car leaves from 1850.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.0.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',2,'Linked, between Courchevel and Méribel','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.1.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',1,'Too little mapped piste to compare grades.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.1.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',3,'Linked, centre of the area','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.2.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',2,'The Mont Vallon gondola above Mottaret has the highest lift top in the valley.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.2.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',4,'Linked by the Olympe gondola only','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.3.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',3,'No pistes; the gondola is ridden both ways.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.3.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',5,'Linked by one gondola and one chair','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.4.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',4,'Too little mapped piste to compare grades.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.4.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',6,'Linked, Belleville valley','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.5.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',5,'The highest share of green and blue among the big resorts.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.5.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',7,'Linked, head of the Belleville valley','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.6.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',6,'Every lift starts above 2,000 m.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.6.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','line',8,'Linked by gondola from the Maurienne','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.7.net'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',7,'The Bouchet chair reaches the highest lift top in the area.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.rows.7.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','areas','note',8,'From the OpenStreetMap lift and piste data (snapshot 20 October 2026) with heights from the Copernicus 90 m elevation model. Green and blue is the share of mapped piste length; drag lifts include platters and T bars as a share of all lifts. Mapped piste is incomplete, so the shares are useful for comparing resorts but not as totals, and they are being checked against the official 2026/27 piste map.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','areas.note'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','heading',0,'Blues reach every valley','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.h2'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','para',0,'The operator counts {{f:F000010}} runs: {{f:F000011}} green, {{f:F000012}} blue, {{f:F000013}} red and {{f:F000014}} black. skiresort.com measures {{f:F000015}} of the piste as easy, {{f:F000016}} as intermediate and {{f:F000017}} as difficult, and lists another {{f:F000003}} of ski routes.',array['F000003','F000010','F000011','F000012','F000013','F000014','F000015','F000016','F000017']::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.paras.0'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','para',1,'In the map data, no pair of sectors needs a black run, and every sector can be reached on green and blue alone. The easy way round usually costs one to three extra lift rides: from the lift bases of Courchevel 1850, Val Thorens takes {{m:easy.c1850.val-thorens|w}} rides on green and blue against {{m:red.c1850.val-thorens|w}} when reds are allowed, and from Les Menuires, Le Praz takes {{m:easy.menuires.le-praz|w}} against {{m:red.menuires.le-praz|w}}.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.paras.1'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','para',2,'That makes the area unusually forgiving for a group of mixed ability, as long as the group meets in the middle. From Mottaret every sector except Orelle is within two lift rides, so the gentler skiers can stay on the blues of the Méribel valley while the others range out to Courchevel or Val Thorens and come back for lunch.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.paras.2'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','para',3,'Stronger skiers have more to find at the top of the lifts than in the run counts. skiresort.com rates the area among its best for experts and freeriders, and the {{f:F000014}} black runs are spread across all three valleys rather than gathered in one corner.',array['F000014']::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.paras.3'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','heading',1,'Lift rides between the areas, and the grade they need','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.matrixTitle'),
('area:les-3-vallees','terrain','note',0,'Rows are where the day starts, columns where it goes. Shaded cells can be reached on green and blue runs, and show the fewest lift rides on those runs. Unshaded cells need at least one red, and show the fewest lift rides with reds allowed. From the OpenStreetMap piste grades, snapshot 20 October 2026; untagged or wrongly tagged runs can distort the result, and each one is being checked against the official map.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','terrain.matrixNote'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','heading',0,'Height keeps the snow','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.h2'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','para',0,'Most of the skiing here is high. The operator puts {{f:F000022}} of the area above 1,800 m. In Val Thorens every lift starts above 2,000 m, and above Orelle the Bouchet chair climbs past 3,200 m. The low ground is short: the lowest lift bases of Le Praz, La Tania and Saint-Martin sit between about 1,250 and 1,400 m.',array['F000022']::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.paras.0'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','para',1,'The weather model behind the snowfall figures covers the centre of the area with one grid cell, so it cannot tell Courchevel from Les Menuires, but it shows plainly what height does. In a typical season between 1991 and 2020, about {{f:F000098}} of snow fell at 1,600 m, {{f:F000100}} at 2,100 m and {{f:F000102}} at 2,600 m.',array['F000098','F000100','F000102']::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.paras.1'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','para',2,'The lower slopes have lost the most. At 1,600 m the typical season fell from {{f:F000099}} in 1961 to 1990 to {{f:F000098}} in 1991 to 2020, and four of the last five seasons sat in the lowest third of the 76 year record. At 2,600 m the fall was smaller, from {{f:F000103}} to {{f:F000102}}, and only two of the last five seasons were that poor.',array['F000098','F000099','F000102','F000103']::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.paras.2'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','para',3,'On this evidence the top half of the area is the safest bet in a thin winter, and Val Thorens and Orelle open first and close last: from {{f:F000037|dm}} to {{f:F000038|dm}} this season, against {{f:F000033|dm}} to {{f:F000034|dm}} for the linked area. The model gives snowfall rather than depth on the ground, and measured depths from weather stations are still being collected.',array['F000033','F000034','F000037','F000038']::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.paras.3'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','heading',1,'Lift heights by sector','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.heightsTitle'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','caption',0,'Lowest lift base to highest lift top in each sector. From OpenStreetMap lift positions and the Copernicus 90 m elevation model, which reads a little low on the highest summits.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.heightsCaption'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','heading',2,'Seasonal snowfall at three heights, 1950 to 2026','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.chartTitle'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','caption',1,'Modelled snowfall from November to April, from the ERA5 reanalysis via the Open-Meteo historical weather API, for the grid cell at 45.25 N, 6.5 E adjusted to each height. Dots are single seasons; lines are 11 season running means. These are model values, not measurements on a piste.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.chartCaption'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',0,'Modelled snowfall from November to April. Dots are single seasons; lines are 11 season running means. Median 1991 to 2020: {{f:F000098}} at 1,600 m, {{f:F000100}} at 2,100 m, {{f:F000102}} at 2,600 m.',array['F000098','F000100','F000102']::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.chartDesc'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',1,'<b>No conditions are reported here yet.</b> Val Thorens and Orelle are due to open on {{f:F000037}} and the linked area on {{f:F000033|dm}}. Until live data arrives, the official sources below give open lifts, pistes and forecasts.',array['F000033','F000037']::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.status'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',2,'Lifts and pistes open','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.items.0.dt'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',3,'<a href="https://www.les3vallees.com/en/live">Les 3 Vallées live status</a>','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.items.0.dd'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',4,'Mountain forecast','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.items.1.dt'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',5,'<a href="https://meteofrance.com/meteo-montagne">Météo-France mountain weather</a>','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.items.1.dd'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',6,'Avalanche danger','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.items.2.dt'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',7,'<a href="https://meteofrance.com/meteo-montagne">Météo-France bulletins</a> for the Vanoise massif, published daily in winter','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.items.2.dd'),
('area:les-3-vallees','snow','line',8,'Terrain beyond the marked pistes is not controlled. The avalanche bulletin and local advice take precedence over anything on this page.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','snow.conditions.safety'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','heading',0,'Does the full pass pay?','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.h2'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','para',0,'A six day adult pass for the whole area costs {{f:F000042}} in high season. The valley passes undercut it by between {{diff:F000042,F000064}} and {{diff:F000042,F000061}}: {{f:F000059}} for the Méribel valley, {{f:F000061}} for Les Menuires and Saint-Martin, and {{f:F000064}} for Val Thorens and Orelle. The gap is less than a single day on the full pass at {{f:F000044}}.',array['F000042','F000044','F000059','F000061','F000064']::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.paras.0'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','para',1,'That arithmetic favours the full pass for almost any week with a day''s travel in it. The case for the valley pass is strongest in Val Thorens, where every lift starts above 2,000 m and the local season runs a fortnight longer at each end.','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.paras.1'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','caption',0,'Valley pass against full pass, adult, 2026/27','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.table.caption'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','line',0,'Méribel valley, six days','{}'::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.table.rows.0.0'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','line',1,'{{f:F000059}}',array['F000059']::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.table.rows.0.1'),
('area:les-3-vallees','pass','line',2,'{{f:F000042}}',array['F000042']::text[],'live','pilot import','pass.table.rows.0.2'),
